  *     X                    halt both arms (drive unaffected)
  *     U                    "this is upright": recapture the tilt reference
  *     ?                    print a "# ..." status line (bench debugging)
+ *   Walking (one "step" = one crank revolution per side = both slabs of that
+ *   side swing once). Moves are self-timed: no D needed while they run.
+ *     W <steps>            walk, + forward / - back, |steps| <= MAX_MOVE_STEPS
+ *     R <deg>              turn in place, multiple of 30, + = left (CCW).
+ *                          Steps = round(|deg| / DEG_PER_TURN_STEP), min 1.
+ *     Q <steps>            raw turn steps (+ = left), for yaw correction
+ *     S / X                also abort a move (ABORT ... stop)
+ *     D with |l|,|r| below the deadband is ignored during a move (the Pi's
+ *                          idle tick); a real D aborts it (ABORT ... drive)
+ *     K <side> <ms>        calibrate ms per step, side 0=L 1=R 2=both (EEPROM)
+ *     Y <deg>              DEG_PER_TURN_STEP (EEPROM)
+ *     M <0|1>              count mode: 1 = crank switches, 0 = timed (EEPROM)
+ *     C                    print "# counts ..." + the CAL line
  *   Uno -> Pi
  *     READY                once after boot (mid-run = the Uno rebooted; arm
  *                          zero is lost, the Pi resets its arm model to 0)
